From f23bb8462da906447c268a6ddf4e6e529bd6b252 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 23:24:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Steam Legacy Collection parity: validated game locator, save
 import, language

- Locator: every candidate must contain GameData/Behavior.iff (a stale Maxis registry key no longer wins over a working Steam install); Steam lookup also reads HKCU SteamPath; a clear message replaces the silent exit when no game is found or -path is wrong.
- Saves: the Legacy Collection writes to Saved Games/Electronic Arts/The Sims 25/UserData*, not its install. Simitone now imports from there when the install is a Legacy Collection.
- Settings: 'Re-import saves from The Sims' (restart) sets Simitone's neighbourhood copies aside (renamed, not deleted) and imports again.
- Language: when never chosen, follow SIMS_LANGUAGE of the installed game.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019q6m8f542cVUMKg755aFtZ
